cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "transport-blender-mcp: a Blender addon and MCP server for prompt-assisted modelling"
abstract: >
  A transport layer for an authoring client rather than a player one, which changes
  the protocol and nothing else: it terminates MCP and triggers work in Blender. A
  fork of BlenderMCP, and the fork exists for one reason -- the parent sends Blender
  data to Supabase, and this opens a local socket and makes no outbound HTTP request
  at all.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/transport-blender-mcp"
keywords:
  - blender
  - model-context-protocol
  - authoring
references:

  - type: software
    title: "BlenderMCP: Blender integration through the Model Context Protocol"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ahuja
        given-names: Siddharth
    url: "https://github.com/ahujasid/blender-mcp"
    notes: >
      The parent this is forked from. The divergence is the whole reason for the fork
      and is a privacy boundary rather than a feature: upstream sends Blender data to
      Supabase, and this one does not leave the machine.

  - type: software
    title: "Model Context Protocol"
    authors:
      - name: Anthropic
    url: "https://modelcontextprotocol.io/"
    notes: "The protocol this terminates; the reason it counts as a transport layer at all."

  - type: software
    title: "Blender"
    authors:
      - name: "Blender Foundation"
    url: "https://www.blender.org/"
    notes: >
      The host the addon runs inside. GPL, and not vendored: the addon is loaded by
      Blender at runtime rather than linked into anything shipped here.
